# Byte-exact checkout contract.
#
# docs/autocad-technician/public-artifact-manifest.json binds every approved
# artifact to the exact byte count and SHA-256 of its repository bytes, and
# scripts/check-private-materials.ps1 verifies each working-tree file against
# that manifest. Any end-of-line translation rewrites those bytes on checkout,
# after which the manifest fails validation and the guard blocks every
# manifest-bound artifact.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system configuration, so a
# default clone on Windows would otherwise convert every tracked text file to
# CRLF and break verification locally while Linux CI still passed.
#
# Disable all end-of-line translation so the working tree matches the
# repository bytes on every platform.
* -text
